{
  "id": "ep440",
  "duration": 34.693,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.04,
      "text": "Apollo 11 astronaut Neil Armstrong flubbed his most famous line.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn Apollo Program (9018112).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Marshall Space Flight Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_Apollo_Program_(9018112).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.833,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.833,
          "end": 4.033,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.04,
      "end": 7.8,
      "text": "Over 500 million people listened to his lunar broadcast live.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "View of Mission Control during lunar surface Apollo 11 EVA (S69-39593).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Johnson Space Center / NA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Mission_Control_during_lunar_surface_Apollo_11_EVA_(S69-39593).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.033,
          "end": 7.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 7.8,
      "end": 11.42,
      "text": "He planned to say, 'one small step for a man'.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Apollo 11 Lunar Lander - 5927 NASA.jpg",
        "credit": "Neil Armstrong",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_11_Lunar_Lander_-_5927_NASA.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 11.433,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.42,
      "end": 13.52,
      "text": "In the broadcast, he dropped the word 'a'.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Telecast of Astronauts Armstrong and Aldrin by the Lunar Module (S69-39563).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Johnson Space Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Telecast_of_Astronauts_Armstrong_and_Aldrin_by_the_Lunar_Module_(S69-39563).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.433,
          "end": 13.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.52,
      "end": 16.26,
      "text": "Without that word, 'man' meant all of humanity.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "A Man on the Moon, AS11-40-5903 (21039130393).jpg",
        "credit": "Neil A. Armstrong",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Man_on_the_Moon,_AS11-40-5903_(21039130393).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.533,
          "end": 16.267,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 16.26,
      "end": 19.7,
      "text": "The speech accidentally compared mankind to mankind.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Apollo 11 plaque closeup on Moon.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_11_plaque_closeup_on_Moon.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.267,
          "end": 19.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.7,
      "end": 23.8,
      "text": "Armstrong and NASA initially claimed radio static swallowed the syllable.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "AS11-37-5528 - Apollo 11 - Apollo 11 Mission image - Neil A. Armstrong inside the Lunar Module after EVA - NARA - 16683662.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown authorUnknown author or not provided",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AS11-37-5528_-_Apollo_11_-_Apollo_11_Mission_image_-_Neil_A._Armstrong_inside_the_Lunar_Module_after_EVA_-_NARA_-_16683662.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.7,
          "end": 21.5,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 21.5,
          "end": 23.8,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.8,
      "end": 27.12,
      "text": "After re-listening to recordings, Armstrong conceded he simply dropped it.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "A11PCf.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A11PCf.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.8,
          "end": 27.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.12,
      "end": 30.64,
      "text": "Official transcripts still place that elusive letter inside brackets.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.133,
          "end": 30.633,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.64,
      "end": 34.343,
      "text": "More than 500 million listeners heard that legendary slip.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn Apollo Program (9018112).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Marshall Space Flight Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_Apollo_Program_(9018112).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.633,
          "end": 34.7,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
